# The FINDINGS panel (src/findings.zig): `<ws>/.mnml/findings/*.md` with
# `severity:` / `status:` frontmatter, one row per report as
# `<SEV> <name>  <title>  <age>`, the shared `sort:` chip, `d` marking
# the selected report resolved in place, and `n` seeding `finding-N.md`.
write .mnml/findings/finding-1.md "---\nseverity: high\nstatus: open\n---\n# Picker panics below 30 cols\n"
write .mnml/findings/r2.md "# Plain report\n\n**Severity:** low\n"
command view.activity_findings
# The panel lives on the left (Rust's placement) in the tree's 30
# columns, where the header keeps only the chips' icons; drag the
# column's divider out to 60 so the rows read in full.
drag 30 5 60 5
wait 400
expect screen contains FINDINGS
expect screen contains "(2 open of 2)"
expect screen contains "HIGH finding-1  Picker panics"
expect screen contains "LOW  r2  Plain report"
# The filter matches the severity word.
key /
type high
expect screen contains "(1 of 2)"
expect screen lacks "Plain report"
key esc
key esc
# Resolve the selected (newest) report: the frontmatter changes on disk,
# the row stays and the open count drops.
key g
key d
wait 400
expect screen contains "(1 open of 2)"
# The sort chip cycles through the palette command; at the shipped panel
# width the chip is icon-only beside the count, so the toast says which.
command findings.sort
expect screen contains "findings: Oldest first"
# `n` seeds the next free name; enter writes the template and opens it.
key n
expect screen contains "finding-2.md"
key enter
expect pane finding-2.md
expect file .mnml/findings/finding-2.md contains "status: open"
